  "articleBody": "Choosing the right trim for your basement can really tie the whole room together! It’s not just about aesthetics; it’s about how well it integrates with your flooring and walls. A common question we get is what trim profile to use. This often depends on the style of your home and the overall look you’re going for in the basement. Do you want something modern and sleek, or more traditional? You also need to figure out how much linear footage you’ll need, and always get a little extra for cuts and mistakes. Don't forget to consider how corners and transitions will be handled – those details make a huge difference in the final look. Should the trim match the floor or wall finish? That’s another common decision point, and there’s no single right answer; it really comes down to your personal preference and the overall design. When you’re making your choice, prioritize trim that complements your existing elements and consider how it will look with your new basement tile. Getting a professional involved can help you make these decisions, especially if you have uneven walls or complex transitions, ensuring a clean, polished finish for your Denver home.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
